{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices","id":119420,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion-Auspices","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-25T16:28:15-07:00","id":119420,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion-Auspices","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/structure-and-moon-signs/\" target=\"_blank\">Find Your Fate Here</a><br /> <br /> Oh my beloved Cahalith, how terrifying you have become. Take me in your arms that will break me again and and again, and show me just how long those teeth really are.<br /> <br /> *ahem* So in regards to the basic summary of each, it's interesting to see what got sharpened with each, but I don't have much to say. I like to see Elodoth clairifed as the business/legal shark of the bunch-if a werewolf is a CEO, it's probably one of them-and while that doesn't help the sometime muddied shared waters between them and the Ithaeur, it still makes them sharper clarified and distinctive. Between this and their gifts from last week, it's neat to see them rip up the world <i>with</i> the world. I will also say that I love the image of an Ithaeur walking down a street with eyes peering out of everything, hands reaching and grabbing and tearing at their prey. I doubt it actually looks like that, but I see it regardless. Everyone else though kind of just got cleaned up in ways I don't feel much like enumerating on, but it's nice to see the edges in the work now.<br /> <br /> As you might guess, I loved the write up on the Cahalith. They've long been a favorite of mine in Werewolf and have only become better as they start wearing stories like a second skin. That pervading feeling of slasher-esque characterization very much continues without overshadowing many of their other faces, particularly in the implementation of their gift...which still does have two things I'm annoyed or confused by, but we'll get back to that.<br /> The write-up does a great job of, once again, creating a greater synergy between the several elements that were originally presented and added onto the Auspices over the year and presnts it in in a unified way that makes sense.Considering the Auspices have take non a number of hats over the years, that's really cool to see the product of all of that get mixed into a truly cohesive whole for once in such a neat package. Even better is giving an synergistic portrayal of the archetypes born from auspice/tribe unions, which for some of these have always been something of a question mark. The entire thing gets me excited to make another Cahalith Iron Master(which, while I've made several hypothetical characters over the years, is definitely the mix I come back to the most), and what's more is that i feel like I really see the picture I've been trying to piece together over the years.<br /> <br /> Now, problems. It's confusion at this point, because I don't know if I'm understanding this right. Both relate to the second use of Prophetic Dreams. One, don't we think that the bonus received after a dream is a little..short to act on? I'm not saying days need to pass here, but in the scene <i>just after</i> a decent night's sleep? Maybe we're purposefully curtailing it a bit, because +3 to anything/beat for fails is kind of potent even for a one off, but still, maybe you should give it at least half a day after? Or at least two to three scenes. Second, am I right in assuming that these dreams are it talks about kind of just generic open ended things that can be defined as the moments call for? Or is it used in relation to the first function, and it's up to the player to draw connections? clarity on both will make me a happy masquer, or at least a less ill-tempered one.<br /> <br /> But no, gripe about the power aside, the presentation is solid and evocative as hell, and it's going to be a a real joy to see everyone else. There's a lot of really cool ideas to get you to start thinking about characters and things to build up on-the ideas that have been brewing upstairs for the past few weeks have definitely just got more sharply defined thanks to to some really clever questions and notation-and now we've moved from a static archetype to a living, breathing, and terrifying(and therefore fun) archetype.<br /> <br /> The legends are alive, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> Next week I stick to my guns and lose a battle very soundly. But at least I get Shakira out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-25-2014, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T16:40:35-07:00","id":119426,"title":"","content":"...I have ha prophetic vision of Brian Blessed as a Cahalith.<br /> <br /> It is a good dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-25-2014, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T16:55:03-07:00","id":119429,"title":"","content":"I'm curious as to the Hunter's Aspect, does this mean that, unlike Vampires who have three aspects of the beast to choose from, Werewolves have one of five based on auspice and ONLY that one?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:00:55-07:00","id":119432,"title":"","content":"I let you take it this time as punishment for last week...or so I tell myself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:21:51-07:00","id":119440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119429#post119429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious as to the Hunter's Aspect, does this mean that, unlike Vampires who have three aspects of the beast to choose from, Werewolves have one of five based on auspice and ONLY that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the way it appears and it makes sense sort of. With the Kindred, the hunter's aspect manifests itself differently depending on the beast within and the temperament at the time. With Uratha, they know their role and regardless of the circumstances, it doesn't change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:28:23-07:00","id":119443,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm certainly relieved to not see a hat trick of Forsaken Saturdays. As for auspice skills, I wonder if werewolves are going to get two free dots of them, as opposed to the one dot of clan attributes, considering they're worth half as much. Or maybe it'll just be specialties again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T17:36:06-07:00","id":119449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119432#post119432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I let you take it this time as punishment for last week...or so I tell myself</div> </div> </div> </div>You were late again, weren't you?<br /> <br /> Don't worry, you'll get it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:07:11-07:00","id":119472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices#post119420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, problems. It's confusion at this point, because I don't know if I'm understanding this right. Both relate to the second use of Prophetic Dreams. One, don't we think that the bonus received after a dream is a little..short to act on? I'm not saying days need to pass here, but in the scene <i>just after</i> a decent night's sleep? Maybe we're purposefully curtailing it a bit, because +3 to anything/beat for fails is kind of potent even for a one off, but still, maybe you should give it at least half a day after? Or at least two to three scenes. Second, am I right in assuming that these dreams are it talks about kind of just generic open ended things that can be defined as the moments call for? Or is it used in relation to the first function, and it's up to the player to draw connections? clarity on both will make me a happy masquer, or at least a less ill-tempered one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're misunderstanding it.<br /> <br /> The ability seems to be:<br /> Storyteller: Something happens!<br /> Pack: Oh crap.<br /> Cahalith Player: I know. Um. My character remembers the dream they had last night, and knows how to handle this...<br /> <br /> The dream seems to be something you essentially make up on the spot, it's not something you have to have, then hope you get to react on it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:10:58-07:00","id":119473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119472#post119472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're misunderstanding it.<br /> <br /> The ability seems to be:<br /> Storyteller: Something happens!<br /> Pack: Oh crap.<br /> Cahalith Player: I know. Um. My character remembers the dream they had last night, and knows how to handle this...<br /> <br /> The dream seems to be something you essentially make up on the spot, it's not something you have to have, then hope you get to react on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I thought it worked, but the wording is bad. It does clearly state that it's usable in the scene after sleep, which has unfortunate implications.<br /> <br /> But again, I thought the way you described it was right, and I now feel more confident in that reading. Masquer pacified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:16:15-07:00","id":119475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices#post119420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, problems. It's confusion at this point, because I don't know if I'm understanding this right. Both relate to the second use of Prophetic Dreams. One, don't we think that the bonus received after a dream is a little..short to act on? I'm not saying days need to pass here, but in the scene <i>just after</i> a decent night's sleep?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're applying an exceedingly narrow reading of &quot;any scene that follows a night in which the character got more than four hours of uninterrupted sleep&quot; - the Uratha have no small number of night-owls, remember.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Aaaaand because my timing appears to have been off, I must add that I enjoy the repeated tidbit about spirits as stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-25-2014, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:30:02-07:00","id":119481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119475#post119475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're applying an exceedingly narrow reading of &amp;quot;any scene that follows a night in which the character got more than four hours of uninterrupted sleep&amp;quot; - the Uratha have no small number of night-owls, remember.</div> </div> </div> </div> Also, a scene that happens three scenes after a night in which the character got four hours of sleep is still very much a scene that follows said night. It doesn't say it has to be the very next scene, just that the scene in which you use it has to happen at some point after you've slept for over four hours. It sounds to me like the only time you can't use it is during a day when you only got an hour-long nap the night before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"atta