"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119482#post119482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being an Exalted fanatic, my reaction was slightly different:<br /> <br /> &quot;OH GOD, THEY'RE RAKSHA. RUN AWAY.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Man geister are <i>ghost stories</i> I don't know where they stock the Bone-and-Cerements Assumption Repellent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T18:53:46-07:00","id":119501,"title":"","content":"This REALLY popped. Wow. That first draft was so jam packed with flavor that I feel like saying screw the Tribes! Just go Auspices hard core!<br /> <br /> This also really emphasizes the Siskur-dah more. Which makes me think that it has a great focus to it. Like... that's the purpose. And the life of the Uratha is one of an endless hunt.<br /> <br /> Damn, I'm stoked for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:12:11-07:00","id":119508,"title":"","content":"So, in case anyone didn't see the comment by Stew, it appears (as of this moment) that Uratha will only have a single hunter's aspect, but they have different types they can take such as war-howler or lore-keeper. This isn't to be confused with the actual ASPECT of the same names. At least that is how I am interpreting the comment and rereading the auspice document.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T19:44:01-07:00","id":119518,"title":"","content":"The Hype is rising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T21:52:06-07:00","id":119566,"title":"","content":"Have to admit, I was never that interested in the Cahalith in Forsaken, but this new write up has made them look much more appealing. If that's a sign of things to come all around, then my excitement for this book is only growing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T22:26:24-07:00","id":119574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119440#post119440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is the way it appears and it makes sense sort of. With the Kindred, the hunter's aspect manifests itself differently depending on the beast within and the temperament at the time. With Uratha, they know their role and regardless of the circumstances, it doesn't change.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does make sense, I'm just wanting to be sure I understand it properly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T22:43:50-07:00","id":119577,"title":"","content":"Irraka and (esp) Ithauer seem to have a clearer style from that preview. Though - as much as I enjoyed the Cahalith writeup, it seemed like it was hitting on the theme of them being unsubtle glory-hounds kind of hard, and then just threw in this mention of introverted HiD ones right at the end. Lots of mention of different ways to live up to lore-keeping; basically no mention of different ways to seek glory. It's still an upgrade from the old, but I'd like more nuance there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T23:43:20-07:00","id":119595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119577#post119577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irraka and (esp) Ithauer seem to have a clearer style from that preview. Though - as much as I enjoyed the Cahalith writeup, it seemed like it was hitting on the theme of them being unsubtle glory-hounds kind of hard, and then just threw in this mention of introverted HiD ones right at the end. Lots of mention of different ways to live up to lore-keeping; basically no mention of different ways to seek glory. It's still an upgrade from the old, but I'd like more nuance there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I prefer the prophet/morale advisor/heart of the pack thing to the whole action hero aspect of the Cahaliths. More nuance would have been nice indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T00:28:43-07:00","id":119613,"title":"","content":"I know it will sound a bit bad, but I see we still come back to <b>Werewolf: The D&amp;D</b> with Auspices. No other supernatural splat have powers working &quot;once per chapter&quot;, especially, as so key as &quot;inborn&quot; splat. Basicly, with this format you all said &quot;Cathalith need to make propthetc dream once a game session&quot;, not more, not less. I assume same goes with other Auscpices so we got &quot;Elodoth need to calm or infuriate some werewolf&quot; and probably &quot;Rahu need to go killing spree&quot;. I know those should be mare leads on roleplaying of Auscpice, but every player want to do &quot;iconic&quot; things of his character at least once a game session otherwise he would choose randomly his X-Splat. So vampire player would want to use his Clan Disciplines, and mage players will favor their Ruling Arcana. But werewolves need to make once ( and only once ) per session Cool Action TM, and it will be the same over and over again - not of five powers from Disciplines or anything more open for multiple scense intepretations like Changlings Kiths Blessings. No, we got the same game scenario each session over and over again. I was hoping that devs would repair that with Idigam Chronicles, but it looks like this was in vain. Practically they said every game session need the same structure because iconic powers of characters are to be used in one schema, most of the time. Very bad Onyx Path, very bad... This is the first thing I don't like as changes in <b>Idigam Chronicles</b>. Or rather - I'm very disapointed it wasn't changed for better.<br /> <br /> Also, First Tounge I see has returned to open use in text, not with classical replacemnts. So as I see, we get for now more of old the same - in parts I would say we should have improvment. But it's only my own opinion. Sad, very sad... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-26-2014, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T00:41:08-07:00","id":119619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119613#post119613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it will sound a bit bad, but I see we still come back to <b>Werewolf: The D&amp;D</b> with Auspices. No other supernatural splat have powers working &quot;once per chapter&quot;, especially, as so key as &quot;inborn&quot; splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please refrain from lying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demon: The Descent Core Rulebook, p90, &quot;Agendas&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules: Each Agenda is associated with its own unique Condition. At the start of each chapter, every character gains the Agenda Conditions of any Agendas he belongs to. Agenda Conditions can generate a Beat once per chapter and have their Resolution effect once per chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Promethean: The Created Core Rulebook, p95, Merits - Elpis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once per game session, the character can use his Elpis ability to gain a supernatural insight concerning a question or topic relevant to his Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: The Lost Core Rulebook, p122, Seemings - Wizened - Kiths</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oracle \u2014 Changelings who, like many imps and goblins, can, in a limited way, see the future. The Oracle\u2019s blessing is Panomancy: the changeling can, once per chapter, tell fortunes using any method she wants \u2014 tea-leaves, cards, bones, a crystal ball or anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken Core Rulebook, p80, Auspices - Rahu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspice Ability: Warrior\u2019s Eye. Once per session, a Rahu can attempt to \u201cread\u201d a foe, determining who is the superior warrior.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf: The Forsaken Core Rulebook, p81, Auspices - Cahalith</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspice Ability: Prophetic Dreams. <b>Once per story</b>, the player may ask the Storyteller for a dream of prophecy, providing some clue about the challenges facing the Cahalith.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-26-2014, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T00:56:42-07:00","id":119624,"title":"","content":"Okay, every once splat before Demon's Conditions - of which I didn't just know as only skeemed the book, waiting for my printed edition.<br /> <br /> Your other examples are particular &quot;once in a gameline&quot; examples, not fundamental, iconic powers. I could give you couple Mage Merits that workd &quot;once per game session&quot;, but they aren't so inherit for the game they are in X-Splats.<br /> <br /> But my argument is still valid - with center on the Hunt and having &quot;iconic powers&quot; being all other that same each session, devs just saying something like this:<br /> <br /> &quot;So every session in Forsaken looks like this:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Cathalith have a dream.</li> <li>Itheru talks with spiritis.</li> <li>Irraka is scouting enemy.</li> <li>Rahu is prepring for combat.</li> <li>Elodoth grants Death Rage on Rahu to kill the beast.&quot;</li> </ol>There could be premutations, but having once per game sessions powers is bad for splats. It was a problem of previous <b>Forsaken</b> line, and as it looks like, they want to makes it once more. All <b>Werewolf</b> sessions should be on the same schema, as it looks like. And it's bad idea for Storytelling game as <i>variety is the spice of life. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-26-2014, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T01:19:11-07:00","id":119630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119613#post119613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it will sound a bit bad, but I see we still come back to <b>Werewolf: The D&amp;D</b> with Auspices. No other supernatural splat have powers working &quot;once per chapter&quot;, especially, as so key as &quot;inborn&quot; splat. Basicly, with this format you all said &quot;Cathalith need to make propthetc dream once a game session&quot;, not more, not less. I assume same goes with other Auscpices so we got &quot;Elodoth need to calm or infuriate some werewolf&quot; and probably &quot;Rahu need to go killing spree&quot;. I know those should be mare leads on roleplaying of Auscpice, but every player want to do &quot;iconic&quot; things of his character at least once a game session otherwise he would choose randomly his X-Splat. So vampire player would want to use his Clan Disciplines, and mage players will favor their Ruling Arcana. But werewolves need to make once ( and only once ) per session Cool Action TM, and it will be the same over and over again - not of five powers from Disciplines or anything more open for multiple scense intepretations like Changlings Kiths Blessings. No, we got the same game scenario each session over and over again. I was hoping that devs would repair that with Idigam Chronicles, but it looks like this was in vain. Practically they said every game session need the same structure because iconic powers of characters are to be used in one schema, most of the time. Very bad Onyx Path, very bad... This is the first thing I don't like as changes in <b>Idigam Chronicles</b>. Or rather - I'm very disapointed it wasn't changed for better.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Stew said in the Comments of the article, you're working off an incorrect assumption here. The equivalent to the Clan Discipline or Ruling Arcana is the Moon Gift, not the once/chapter power.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure where the 'Werewolf: the D&amp;D' comment comes from either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T01:36:05-07:00","id":119637,"title":"","content":"Now I'm kind of sad to know that the Dreaming Moon Gifts won't get a huge facelift and shine for the world to see along with this refocusing of Cahalith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T02:22:44-07:00","id":119646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119630#post119630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Stew said in the Comments of the article, you're working off an incorrect assumption here. The equivalent to the Clan Discipline or Ruling Arcana is the Moon Gift, not the once/chapter power.<br /> <br /> I'm not entirely sure where the 'Werewolf: the D&amp;D' comment comes from either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... An argument could be made that the Auspices are effectively Classes, such as Warrior, Bard, Shaman, Rogue, etc. But the same could be done for Vampire and Mage very easily enough.<br /> <br /> It's a useful tool to have archetypes available for players to better define their characters, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T03:21:19-07:00","id":119653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119646#post119646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh... An argument could be made that the Auspices are effectively Classes, such as Warrior, Bard, Shaman, Rogue, etc. But the same could be done for Vampire and Mage very easily enough.<br /> <br /> It's a useful tool to have archetypes available for players to better define their characters, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there aren't like in <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Mage</b>. Problem isn't in Archetypes themselves, my problem is in working of <b>powers</b> for the archetypes. Now powers makes real gameplay all the same, each play sessions. Basiclly, they shut down archetype exploration saying &quot;all Cathalith will spend days in dreaming for visions&quot;. In <b>Mage</b> you only have hints like &quot;Moros will want to speak with the dead and resolve the anchors&quot;. You don't have &quot;once per game session you can be awesome&quot; powers to cement it. Suggestion, not a statement of fact by mechanics<br /> <br /> Each session Cathalith will want to have mystical visions. Each session Elodoth player will look to put someone in Death Rage state. Each session Itheru will command spirits ( a bit my assumption, based on previous powers in corebooks ). Thin is - in <b>Mage</b> and <b>Vampire</b> yout Clan or Path don't make you do anything. Yes, you got Clan weakness you must take in account, but scence are stired by characters ideas, not the power they should use on each game session.<br /> <br /> It is problem for me, as I don't want all of game sessions to resolve around of Hunt. Most, yeah, sure. But every player wants to make his character cool at least one each game session. And devs just said &quot;all of you can be cool by this way. There are other ways, but this is the best and this you will do over, and over again, till you die in battle you will always look for,&quot; Becuase, as it seems, Werewolf is like D&amp;D game, still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-26-2014, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T06:29:43-07:00","id":119692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119653#post119653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, there aren't like in <b>Vampire</b> and <b>Mage</b>. Problem isn't in Archetypes themselves, my problem is in working of <b>powers</b> for the archetypes. Now powers makes real gameplay all the same, each play sessions. Basiclly, they shut down archetype exploration saying &quot;all Cathalith will spend days in dreaming for visions&quot;. In <b>Mage</b> you only have hints like &quot;Moros will want to speak with the dead and resolve the anchors&quot;. You don't have &quot;once per game session you can be awesome&quot; powers to cement it. Suggestion, not a statement of fact by mechanics<br /> <br /> Each session Cathalith will want to have mystical visions. Each session Elodoth player will look to put someone in Death Rage state. Each session Itheru will command spirits ( a bit my assumption, based on previous powers in corebooks ). Thin is - in <b>Mage</b> and <b>Vampire</b> yout Clan or Path don't make you do anything. Yes, you got Clan weakness you must take in account, but scence are stired by characters ideas, not the power they should use on each game session.<br /> <br /> It is problem for me, as I don't want all of game sessions to resolve around of Hunt. Most, yeah, sure. But every player wants to make his character cool at least one each game session. And devs just said &quot;all of you can be cool by this way. There are other ways, but this is the best and this you will do over, and over again, till you die in battle you will always look for,&quot; Becuase, as it seems, Werewolf is like D&amp;D game, still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a major difference between 'can use' and 'must use'. If a Storm Lord Cahalith sees his visions in, say, how he will die this time, I doubt it matters in every session what he saw in his dreams. They are things the player can use, that relates to their auspice role. Not the sole thing the auspice can do, there are gifts after all, and unique ways the blessing can manifest.<br /> <br /> One part is also that unlike other WoD games, the pack IS the thing for werewolf. In Vampire the PCs can be a loyal coterie, sure, but they can also fight against one another. They and Mages are more like a human gang as a group. Uratha -need- a pack, and as such, their auspices are more DnD based for sure, but for a reason. They are roles in a group, and roles I think a lot of players WANT to play out. And it doesn't always have to be the Hunt that the roles are used for. Ithauer can seek spirits for other things than the hunt, Elodoth mostly do stuff pre or post hunt and Cahalith might spend time honing their stories.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T07:18:41-07:00","id":119721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119692#post119692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a major difference between 'can use' and 'must use'. If a Storm Lord Cahalith sees his visions in, say, how he will die this time, I doubt it matters in every session what he saw in his dreams. They are things the player can use, that relates to their auspice role. Not the sole thing the auspice can do, there are gifts after all, and unique ways the blessing can manifest.<br /> <br /> One part is also that unlike other WoD games, the pack IS the thing for werewolf. In Vampire the PCs can be a loyal coterie, sure, but they can also fight against one another. They and Mages are more like a human gang as a group. Uratha -need- a pack, and as such, their auspices are more DnD based for sure, but for a reason. They are roles in a group, and roles I think a lot of players WANT to play out.</div> </div> </div> </div>You see, I understand this logic - I don't agree with this, but now I could understand why Forsaken is game as it is. I was thinking devs wanted to broad the game to others ways of play, but with Auspices they just do more of the same. In nice, cool, exciting way - but not fixing self imposed limits on they Auspices from previous version of game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119692#post119692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it doesn't always have to be the Hunt that the roles are used for. Ithauer can seek spirits for other things than the hunt, Elodoth mostly do stuff pre or post hunt and Cahalith might spend time honing their stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>But nothing meaningful. You must leave Auspices blessings to Hunt, as it is most important, always. I'm <b>Mage</b> ST and I very like variety on sessions. Let's say I want to run bloody pack negotiations on territory, broken off by some random monster attack.<br /> <br /> Elodoth can use only once per session his calming Death Rage power. So even there are two packs, with 4 memebers each, and half of them are gone to Death Rage by exchange of insults - he can choose only one instance of using it. But even then he wouldn't use it, as probably player is sensing there will be more to session later. &quot;Once per session&quot; powers are bad for good storytelling, becuase players wouldn't want to take chances with them. At least half solving this problem would be to useable by the cost of Willpower or by waitng 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'all need to stop feeding the troll. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm no troll, Sir. I'm one of main posters in<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/112231-werewolf-as-a-roleplay-game-making-it-click\"> I want to love <b>Forsaken</b></a> game topic. I really like the changes to this game till now. Just Auspices come to me as &quot;more of the same&quot; and once more too D&amp;D - if I want to play D&amp;D, I play D&amp;D, not horror game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-26-2014, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T08:00:04-07:00","id":119745,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the D&amp;D comparison is so off base that it sounds like you're doing nothing more than manufacturing a reason to complain instead of enjoying the game for what it actually is (or in this case will be).<br /> <br /> The innate Auspice powers (as opposed to all the other Auspice bonuses they have) are once per session? So... that's like one Class mechanic from one edition of D&amp;D. Boohoo. You might as well be arguing that equipment is modeled by giving you bonuses, which is how D&amp;D does things, so the whole nWOD is only good for murderhobo dungeon crawling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T09:11:07-07:00","id":119778,"title":"","content":"Plus, as said before, you don't need to be in a hunt to have dreams. You don't need to be in a hunt to deal with spirits. Just because your powers are useful in a hunt, that doesn't mean it can't be used for personal affairs, and it doesn't mean you are shoehorned in your role. There are plenty of ways to use your auspice power for things other than the hunt, and that's for some Gifts too.<br /> And if I understood well, your Elodoth can also use his power to end Kuruth during a social situation where two werewolves might be fighting each other for any kind of dispute, be it pack versus pack, be it pack member vs pack member, and things like that.<br /> <br /> Exalted Solar Castes is much similar, and possibly even more similar to &quot;D&amp;D&quot;. Hell, you could actually play Exalted in a Dungeon Crawler style. But not all Dawn Caste are &quot;Big stupid fighters&quot;. One might have been a smith and have high Crafts. Or it might be a Dawn Sorcerer. Or a nobleman with high social skills. A Twilight Caste might be a sage warrior.<br /> Still, all Exalted Castes have a &quot;role&quot; power. The Dawn is good at making people back down, the Eclipse is good at dealing with social enconters thanks to supernatural pledges.<br /> <br /> You have powers, and it's your choice what to do with them.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> On the same example, a Rahu could well be a master of rituals. It might not be as good as an Ithaeur, but hey, rites are rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T09:17:27-07:00","id":119785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119778#post119778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the same example, a Rahu could well be a master of rituals. It might not be as good as an Ithaeur, but hey, rites are rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although one must say that is not popular among conservative Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1999-wolf","name":"Wolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1999_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T09:56:49-07:00","id":119805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119721#post119721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You see, I understand this logic - I don't agree with this, but now I could understand why Forsaken is game as it is. I was thinking devs wanted to broad the game to others ways of play, but with Auspices they just do more of the same. In nice, cool, exciting way - but not fixing self imposed limits on they Auspices from previous version of game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that was ever the point to fix the 'limits', to be honest. With Vampires and Mages, their ability to choose which path they took has always been part of what I consider theur humanity. Even if vampires are a bit dofferent, they still have such choices. To werewolves, creatures of much more inhumanity, the auspices feed into the inhumanity. Unlike other splats, the auspice is their calling, their tie to Luna. It is something very personal to them, and it goes with their nature. Besides, there are so many ways that an auspice can manifest. Their power is only guidelines to what you can do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119721#post119721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But nothing meaningful. You must leave Auspices blessings to Hunt, as it is most important, always. I'm <b>Mage</b> ST and I very like variety on sessions. Let's say I want to run bloody pack negotiations on territory, broken off by some random monster attack.<br /> <br /> Elodoth can use only once per session his calming Death Rage power. So even there are two packs, with 4 memebers each, and half of them are gone to Death Rage by exchange of insults - he can choose only one instance of using it. But even then he wouldn't use it, as probably player is sensing there will be more to session later. &quot;Once per session&quot; powers are bad for good storytelling, becuase players wouldn't want to take chances with them. At least half solving this problem would be to useable by the cost of Willpower or by waitng 24 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then don't -have- anything like the Hunt in the session. Yes, a wolf must hunt, but no predator EVER goes hunting just for the sake of hunting. The Hunt is called Sacred for a reason, it is something special, something more than a simple killing. As such, the hunt should not be a common occurence in the session, more like a culmination of one 'season' as it were. If anything, the sessions should be spent figuring out what they have to hunt, how to hunt and preparing for the hunt. This can easily span many sessions, and have a lot of minor plots on the side. Things like managing things with WB and human packmates, making deals with other packmates. Killing minor threats, etc.<br /> <br /> As for the situation, the Elodoth using the ability might prefer to focus on keep good relations between the packs despite there being more to the session. Or he might not, it's more a player choice than yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T11:15:04-07:00","id":119844,"title":"","content":"Pretty much every session of Werewolf involves a hunt just like pretty much every session of Mage involves a mystery and pretty much every session of Demon involves spying. This seems like more of a feature then a bug. Hunt has a lot of room for variety inside it. It's not like wolves specifically go pheasant shooting the exact same way every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T11:17:24-07:00","id":119847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119721#post119721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elodoth can use only once per session his calming Death Rage power. So even there are two packs, with 4 memebers each, and half of them are gone to Death Rage by exchange of insults - he can choose only one instance of using it. But even then he wouldn't use it, as probably player is sensing there will be more to session later. &quot;Once per session&quot; powers are bad for good storytelling, becuase players wouldn't want to take chances with them. At least half solving this problem would be to useable by the cost of Willpower or by waitng 24 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're half right. The power is starting or stopping Death Rage.<br /> <br /> Considering you don't know what Death Rage does in the game, you might be jumping the gun in predicting how werewolves will start it, and whether they'll want to or not.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has always been about hunting. In Forsaken, it was hunt or be hunted, and now it's the wolf must hunt. The hunt is an important part of werewolf lifestyle, but as the developers have pointed out, it is not the only aspect of their life. You could run Werewolf similar to D&amp;D, but that would just be you. Nothing we've seen in any of the blogs has implied anything of the sort. And considering Hunter the Vigil actually -is- mostly about fighting monsters and is not D&amp;D, you probably don't have to worry about Idigam Chronicles doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T11:28:26-07:00","id":119854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119844#post119844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every session of Werewolf involves a hunt just like pretty much every session of Mage involves a mystery and pretty much every session of Demon involves spying. This seems like more of a feature then a bug. Hunt has a lot of room for variety inside it. It's not like wolves specifically go pheasant shooting the exact same way every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Wyrdhamster is thinking is that all sessions will be about the Sacred Hunt, rather than hunting in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T11:31:01-07:00","id":119856,"title":"","content":"They present an example to the contrary right in the title, though. The Idigam aren't anyone's sacred hunt and they go on the cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T13:01:52-07:00","id":119912,"title":"","content":"I've played lots of Cahalith, and I've never felt restricted to doing one sort of action each game, nor did I feel like I missed out on not doing so.<br /> <br /> THe new presentation is an expansion, not a restriction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T23:48:36-07:00","id":120214,"title":"","content":"In general I liked the new write up. Auspice was something that desperately needed expansion in the old Forsaken rulebook. So I'm glad that the new core seems to be emphasizing them a great deal more and making them more obviously equivalent to Clans from Vampire.<br /> <br /> As a starting point I'd like to say that I've never really &quot;got&quot; the Cahalith before. The old fluff seemed to go with the Storyteller angle a lot, which never really inspired me. With this new write up I enjoy about half of what's talked about.<br /> <br /> The focus on the Cahalith as prophets was excellent, really liked it. Love all the talk about them being everything from bombastic prophets to doom-tellers to academic like historians (is science) I felt that gave a lot of range of character for the Auspice. I think the stuff about how they actually interact with and relate to the concept of &quot;stories&quot; needs to be clarified a bit personally, but maybe their Moon Gifts might add more flavour in that regard.<br /> <br /> I'm actually kinda surprised how much I like this aspect actually. As a lot of the fluff here (we'll have to wait and see on the crunch) is not a million miles away from the wishy-washy stuff about &quot;fate&quot; and &quot;story narrative shapes reality&quot; in Changeling that turns me complete off that game.<br /> <br /> The stuff I don't love is the &quot;larger then life action hero&quot; vibe the other half of the write up keeps pushing. I think it kinda detracts from the other half of the write up. The tiny almost disclaimer like bits about &quot;but not all Cahalith are extrovert&quot; and &quot;but this does not mean they can't be subtle&quot; really, really don't ring true with the rest of the write up and seem almost tacked on.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't like the idea that a group of beings that are tied to prophecy (which is heavily involved with metaphor and interpretation), dreams (which are often used in media and fiction via symbolism and subconscious drives) and stories (which can be as crass or subtle in nature as the storyteller in question decides the tale should be) don't really have a grasp of nuance. Its kinda jarring.<br /> <br /> When this aspect is tied a little more into the prophet fluff I warm to it a little. A Cahalith going out of his/her way to make sure that their prey dies in a way they foresaw in a dream or the idea of taking on the &quot;narrative&quot; role of Death in the prey's story is interesting. I think the Predatory Aspect of Monstrous backs this aspect up a bit and could be used very interestingly by an ST and player who are very much in sinc with the idea.<br /> <br /> So basically as a first draft, its good, I'd like to see some revision after redlines to tease out the more subtle aspects to do with how Cahalith see stories, dreams and spirits interacting a bit more perhaps. Likewise a little more effort in expanding the explanation of &quot;non extrovert&quot; and &quot;subtle&quot; Cahalith would not go amiss.<br /> <br /> As for Wyrdhamsters point:<br /> <br /> His/Her comparison between the Auspice ability and Vampire disciplines is not really a valid one. As that's not an accurate comparison, an Auspice blessing is more comparable with the bonus attribute dot and the unique Clan Bane that each clan gives a character.<br /> <br /> An even better comparison would be between Auspice and a Demons Agenda which gives a similar once a chapter ability or about comparable power. As a person who has played in a Demon game, these once a Chapter abilities really do not define a characters role in the game or group on a session by session basis. They come up when its appropriate for them to do so due to in game events or character choices.<br /> <br /> The unique Moon Gift that each Auspice is getting is the equivalent of an &quot;unique&quot; Clan discipline e.g. Auspex for the Mekhet. The Shadow and Hunt Gifts would be comparable to &quot;common&quot; (Vigor, Resilience, Celerity) and I imagine the Tribe Gifts will be comparable to &quot;uncommon&quot; (Animalism, Obfuscate) disciplines that appear in different clans.<br /> <br /> What I will say is that his point has merit if you have a player group that is thinking in a default tactical D&amp;D 4th edition mentality. As of course the optimum thing is to use the Cahalith Auspice Blessing to give +3 when the group needs it the next night! That's one way to play any roleplay game, its not my cup of tea, and I don't think it helps reinforce the WoD's themes and play style, but its an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","user":"Hawthorn","date":". 04-27-2014, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T23:55:44-07:00","id":120219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119778#post119778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, as said before, you don't need to be in a hunt to have dreams. You don't need to be in a hunt to deal with spirits. Just because your powers are useful in a hunt, that doesn't mean it can't be used for personal affairs, and it doesn't mean you are shoehorned in your role. There are plenty of ways to use your auspice power for things other than the hunt, and that's for some Gifts too.<br /> And if I understood well, your Elodoth can also use his power to end Kuruth during a social situation where two werewolves might be fighting each other for any kind of dispute, be it pack versus pack, be it pack member vs pack member, and things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading a bit more in this topic I see it. But still, Elodoth power would make great use for negotiation type session, but it's limited only to &quot;usable once per session&quot;. Not dramatic as first I assumed, but still it's a wast and killing good ideas thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119778#post119778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted Solar Castes is much similar, and possibly even more similar to &quot;D&amp;D&quot;. Hell, you could actually play Exalted in a Dungeon Crawler style. But not all Dawn Caste are &quot;Big stupid fighters&quot;. One might have been a smith and have high Crafts. Or it might be a Dawn Sorcerer. Or a nobleman with high social skills. A Twilight Caste might be a sage warrior.<br /> Still, all Exalted Castes have a &quot;role&quot; power. The Dawn is good at making people back down, the Eclipse is good at dealing with social enconters thanks to supernatural pledges.<br /> <br /> You have powers, and it's your choice what to do with them.<br /> (...)<br /> <br /> On the same example, a Rahu could well be a master of rituals. It might not be as good as an Ithaeur, but hey, rites are rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know Exalted ( yet, always wanted to try it ), but I don't have a problem with thinking character outside or on egde of archetype, I got a problem with power working only once per session and by this, imposing a game bit. As I thinks, the &quot;cost of Willpower&quot; or &quot;till the next moonrise&quot; would solve probably most of mine problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119805#post119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that was ever the point to fix the 'limits', to be honest. With Vampires and Mages, their ability to choose which path they took has always been part of what I consider theur humanity. Even if vampires are a bit dofferent, they still have such choices. To werewolves, creatures of much more inhumanity, the auspices feed into the inhumanity. Unlike other splats, the auspice is their calling, their tie to Luna. It is something very personal to them, and it goes with their nature. Besides, there are so many ways that an auspice can manifest. Their power is only guidelines to what you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ana, you shuould write selling materials for <b>Werewolf</b> - this is very helpful. Remebering that werewolves <b>should</b> be more inhuman, even from vampires. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119805#post119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then don't -have- anything like the Hunt in the session. Yes, a wolf must hunt, but no predator EVER goes hunting just for the sake of hunting. The Hunt is called Sacred for a reason, it is something special, something more than a simple killing. As such, the hunt should not be a common occurence in the session, more like a culmination of one 'season' as it were. If anything, the sessions should be spent figuring out what they have to hunt, how to hunt and preparing for the hunt. This can easily span many sessions, and have a lot of minor plots on the side. Things like managing things with WB and human packmates, making deals with other packmates. Killing minor threats, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so let's say that Sacred Hunt is thing to be used at the end of several sessions, like 7th, let's say. We could use Auspices from time to time to other things - but outside the Elodoth they are mostly suited to Sacred Hunt. So what - we give payers &quot;once per session&quot; powers, but they want use it if on, let's say 3rd sesion, there is recon and mostly Irraka is in charge, so our Rahu wouldn't smash things?<br /> <br /> As for the situation, the Elodoth using the ability might prefer to focus on keep good relations between the packs despite there being more to the session. Or he might not, it's more a player choice than yours.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119844#post119844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every session of Werewolf involves a hunt just like pretty much every session of Mage involves a mystery and pretty much every session of Demon involves spying. This seems like more of a feature then a bug. Hunt has a lot of room for variety inside it. It's not like wolves specifically go pheasant shooting the exact same way every time.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119847#post119847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're half right. The power is starting or stopping Death Rage.<br /> <br /> Considering you don't know what Death Rage does in the game, you might be jumping the gun in predicting how werewolves will start it, and whether they'll want to or not.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119778#post119778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, as said before, you don't need to be in a hunt to have dreams. You don't need to be in a hunt to deal with spirits. Just because your powers are useful in a hunt, that doesn't mean it can't be used for personal affairs, and it doesn't mean you are shoehorned in your role. There are plenty of ways to use your auspice power for things other than the hunt, and that's for some Gifts too.<br /> And if I understood well, your Elodoth can also use his power to end Kuruth during a social situation where two werewolves might be fighting each other for any kind of dispute, be it pack versus pack, be it pack member vs pack member, and things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>After reading a bit more in this topic I see it. But still, Elodoth power would make great use for negotiation type session, but it's limited only to &quot;usable once per session&quot;. Not dramatic as first I assumed, but still it's a wast and killing good ideas thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119778#post119778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted Solar Castes is much similar, and possibly even more similar to &quot;D&amp;D&quot;. Hell, you could actually play Exalted in a Dungeon Crawler style. But not all Dawn Caste are &quot;Big stupid fighters&quot;. One might have been a smith and have high Crafts. Or it might be a Dawn Sorcerer. Or a nobleman with high social skills. A Twilight Caste might be a sage warrior.<br /> Still, all Exalted Castes have a &quot;role&quot; power. The Dawn is good at making people back down, the Eclipse is good at dealing with social enconters thanks to supernatural pledges.<br /> <br /> You have powers, and it's your choice what to do with them.<br /> (...)<br /> <br /> On the same example, a Rahu could well be a master of rituals. It might not be as good as an Ithaeur, but hey, rites are rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know Exalted ( yet, always wanted to try it ), but I don't have a problem with thinking character outside or on egde of archetype, I got a problem with power working only once per session and by this, imposing a game bit. As I thinks, the &quot;cost of Willpower&quot; or &quot;till the next moonrise&quot; would solve probably most of mine problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119805#post119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that was ever the point to fix the 'limits', to be honest. With Vampires and Mages, their ability to choose which path they took has always been part of what I consider theur humanity. Even if vampires are a bit dofferent, they still have such choices. To werewolves, creatures of much more inhumanity, the auspices feed into the inhumanity. Unlike other splats, the auspice is their calling, their tie to Luna. It is something very personal to them, and it goes with their nature. Besides, there are so many ways that an auspice can manifest. Their power is only guidelines to what you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ana, you shuould write selling materials for <b>Werewolf</b> - this is very helpful. Remebering that werewolves <b>should</b> be more inhuman, even from vampires. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119805#post119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then don't -have- anything like the Hunt in the session. Yes, a wolf must hunt, but no predator EVER goes hunting just for the sake of hunting. The Hunt is called Sacred for a reason, it is something special, something more than a simple killing. As such, the hunt should not be a common occurence in the session, more like a culmination of one 'season' as it were. If anything, the sessions should be spent figuring out what they have to hunt, how to hunt and preparing for the hunt. This can easily span many sessions, and have a lot of minor plots on the side. Things like managing things with WB and human packmates, making deals with other packmates. Killing minor threats, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkay, so let's say that Sacred Hunt is thing to be used at the end of several sessions, like 7th, let's say. We could use Auspices from time to time to other things - but outside the Elodoth they are mostly suited to Sacred Hunt. So what - we give payers &quot;once per session&quot; powers, but they want use it if on, let's say 3rd sesion, there is recon and mostly Irraka is in charge, so our Rahu wouldn't smash things?<br /> <br /> As for the situation, the Elodoth using the ability might prefer to focus on keep good relations between the packs despite there being more to the session. Or he might not, it's more a player choice than yours.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119844#post119844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every session of Werewolf involves a hunt just like pretty much every session of Mage involves a mystery and pretty much every session of Demon involves spying. This seems like more of a feature then a bug. Hunt has a lot of room for variety inside it. It's not like wolves specifically go pheasant shooting the exact same way every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>[QUOTE=nofather;n119847]<br /> <br /> You're half right. The power is starting or stopping Death Rage.<br /> <br /> Considering you don't know what Death Rage does in the game, you might be jumping the gun in predicting how werewolves will start it, and whether they'll want to or not.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon_