are a bit dofferent, they still have such choices. To werewolves, creatures of much more inhumanity, the auspices feed into the inhumanity. Unlike other splats, the auspice is their calling, their tie to Luna. It is something very personal to them, and it goes with their nature. Besides, there are so many ways that an auspice can manifest. Their power is only guidelines to what you can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ana, you shuould write selling materials for <b>Werewolf</b> - this is very helpful. Remebering that werewolves <b>should</b> be more inhuman, even from vampires. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119805#post119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then don't -have- anything like the Hunt in the session. Yes, a wolf must hunt, but no predator EVER goes hunting just for the sake of hunting. The Hunt is called Sacred for a reason, it is something special, something more than a simple killing. As such, the hunt should not be a common occurence in the session, more like a culmination of one 'season' as it were. If anything, the sessions should be spent figuring out what they have to hunt, how to hunt and preparing for the hunt. This can easily span many sessions, and have a lot of minor plots on the side. Things like managing things with WB and human packmates, making deals with other packmates. Killing minor threats, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOkay, so let's say that Sacred Hunt is thing to be used at the end of several sessions, like 7th, let's say. We could use Auspices from time to time to other things - but outside the Elodoth they are mostly suited to Sacred Hunt. So what - we give payers &quot;once per session&quot; powers, but they want use it if on, let's say 3rd sesion, there is recon and mostly Irraka is in charge, so our Rahu wouldn't smash things?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119805#post119805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the situation, the Elodoth using the ability might prefer to focus on keep good relations between the packs despite there being more to the session. Or he might not, it's more a player choice than yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but giving &quot;once per session&quot; power just kills a good, or t least interesting storyline with this. Player can risk or not - if power would more easier to use, you as ST can assume plaer rather will use it, and by this, werewolf negotiation scene looks as more possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119844#post119844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much every session of Werewolf involves a hunt just like pretty much every session of Mage involves a mystery and pretty much every session of Demon involves spying. This seems like more of a feature then a bug. Hunt has a lot of room for variety inside it. It's not like wolves specifically go pheasant shooting the exact same way every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most session of Mage involve Mystery. But there are also personal dramas or political things. Or even &quot;cops are after us and we don't use magic&quot;. For now Auspices says more &quot;Cathalith need a dream once a session&quot; kind of thing than &quot;Cathalith could have prothetic dreams&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119847#post119847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're half right. The power is starting or stopping Death Rage.<br /> <br /> Considering you don't know what Death Rage does in the game, you might be jumping the gun in predicting how werewolves will start it, and whether they'll want to or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we know how it works before and how changes are looking now, so I don't thing there will be change in &quot;anger trigers Death Rage&quot;. But yes, I make here assumption none the less. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119847#post119847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf has always been about hunting. In Forsaken, it was hunt or be hunted, and now it's the wolf must hunt. The hunt is an important part of werewolf lifestyle, but as the developers have pointed out, it is not the only aspect of their life. You could run Werewolf similar to D&amp;D, but that would just be you. Nothing we've seen in any of the blogs has implied anything of the sort. And considering Hunter the Vigil actually -is- mostly about fighting monsters and is not D&amp;D, you probably don't have to worry about Idigam Chronicles doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Till now I would agree with you. But then Auspices power states baldly &quot;your werewolf will hunt every session&quot;. <b>Every</b> game session to make cool actions your PC could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119854#post119854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what Wyrdhamster is thinking is that all sessions will be about the Sacred Hunt, rather than hunting in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that Sacred Hunt will be from time to time, but yes, it looks like werewolf all the time hunts. I understand this assumption, but with Auspices mechanics, I see it's too much locked in. My bloody pack negoations only states this - I easily can see situation like teritorial sdespiute between packs and hunting on one another isn't solution. Would love the machincs that even slightly support this and other game sessions materials, not hunting only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=119856#post119856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They present an example to the contrary right in the title, though. The Idigam aren't anyone's sacred hunt and they go on the cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me there isn't very diffrance bettwen hunt and Sacred Hunt. From the looks on mechanics, Auspices will work the same with one and another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T00:46:24-07:00","id":120229,"title":"","content":"It still seems like you're blowing a single once-per session power (that's free!) completely out of proportion for the amount of effect it will have on game-play. The innate Auspice power is one thing they get. It is not the be all and end all of a character. It not coming up in a given session is no more important than their Moon Gift not coming up that session or their Predatory Aspect not coming up. <br /> <br /> Can you actually explain why this is a bad thing in a fashion that isn't fairly circularly reliant on the base-line assumption that &quot;once per session&quot; style powers are bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T05:49:49-07:00","id":120301,"title":"","content":"wyrdhamster, I'd posit that if the Auspice Abilities are as jarring in actual play as you describe, that they'll shake out during playtesting. Now, I don't know what the plan is for that yet, but that's when we'll find out what's jarring in the system (or, conversely, not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T08:41:11-07:00","id":120357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120301#post120301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wyrdhamster, I'd posit that if the Auspice Abilities are as jarring in actual play as you describe, that they'll shake out during playtesting. Now, I don't know what the plan is for that yet, but that's when we'll find out what's jarring in the system (or, conversely, not).</div> </div> </div> </div>Will be there playtests? As I get to heard the book is coming up in July...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T08:43:28-07:00","id":120358,"title":"","content":"It's coming out in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">September</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T08:44:44-07:00","id":120359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120357#post120357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will be there playtests? As I get to heard the book is coming up in July...</div> </div> </div> </div>Check the Schedule page on the Onyx Path Website. Idigam's been moved to September. Not a bad thing, the more time they have to playtest and polish the game and get fan feedback the better. Strix stayed open to fan feedback for about a couple of months after it should and I'm sure the book would not have been as good if they had not extended that period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:48:36-07:00","id":120388,"title":"","content":"Simple point to Wyrdhamster: I think you gotta know what exactly you're hunting in order to call down the Sacred Hunt on them. So, the first steps would be figuring out what the heck is going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T11:33:58-07:00","id":120426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120359#post120359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check the Schedule page on the Onyx Path Website. Idigam's been moved to September. Not a bad thing, the more time they have to playtest and polish the game and get fan feedback the better. Strix stayed open to fan feedback for about a couple of months after it should and I'm sure the book would not have been as good if they had not extended that period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will we see rules for playtests? I'm a bit worried, cause I was thinking on starting my <b>Forsaken</b> game about <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/115874-wolves-of-hell-brainstorming-forsaken-inferno-game-possibly-idigam-chronicles\">Hell Hounds</a></b> in July. And really was counting on those new Wolf-Blooded rules to start...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120388#post120388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple point to Wyrdhamster: I think you gotta know what exactly you're hunting in order to call down the Sacred Hunt on them. So, the first steps would be figuring out what the heck is going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSimple, and obvious point, yes. But I will still treat this as a pre-Hunt. What's with things outside of it? For example my packs negotiations? I could see that Auspices are more open than I think so, but still my most concern is that to not force Hunt always on game with awesome powers for it ( even if I know Gifts are for this also ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-27-2014, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:24:49-07:00","id":120458,"title":"","content":"at least 60% of the usual antagonists which populate Forsaken can't be done away with simple applications of violence. Discorporate a spirit without another measure, and it'll be ridding people within a few more weeks. Leave a locus unchecked and watch how the balance goes to hell. You could attempt to destroy it, but without changing the underlying resonance of the place, it's gonna be respawned. Negotiations is also the whole schtick of Elodoth and Ithaeur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:29:30-07:00","id":120461,"title":"","content":"Wyrdhampster, you're taking the word &quot;hunt&quot; too literally. Just because a werewolf is not tracking down prey to kill and eat does not mean they aren't &quot;hunting&quot;. The Uratha view everything in terms of a predator/prey relationship. Pack negotiations are themselves a kind of hunt - the aggressor socially harrying their opposition, their social prey. The same goes for any interaction the Uratha have. The wolf must hunt, not only because the siskur-dah is a sacred calling, but because everything the wolf does is a metaphorical hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T12:50:34-07:00","id":120470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120461#post120461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrdhampster, you're taking the word &quot;hunt&quot; too literally. Just because a werewolf is not tracking down prey to kill and eat does not mean they aren't &quot;hunting&quot;. The Uratha view everything in terms of a predator/prey relationship. Pack negotiations are themselves a kind of hunt - the aggressor socially harrying their opposition, their social prey. The same goes for any interaction the Uratha have. The wolf must hunt, not only because the siskur-dah is a sacred calling, but because everything the wolf does is a metaphorical hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so if I get it too literally, why each Tribe has <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;favored enemy&quot;</a>? Only Iron Masters have thing I could assume is concept - they are hunting organisations, religions, etc. - but rest have spirits or spirits based hybrids ( werewolves are also this one ). What can I thought other from the info we get?<br /> <br /> If we get something like that Tribes takes abstracs also as they Hunts, I could see something like Strom Lords hunting imputyies in society, Blood Talons weak elements, etc. Then &quot;social hunting&quot; Strom Lord that runs homeless shelter would have sens and show &quot;social hunting&quot;, making also character that aren't all about going after monsters in the night.<br /> <br /> What I mean, basiclly, is this - I see there is huge empathies on Uratha spirit side and duties. But there isn't very much hilighted they flesh/human side a bit. I know it's action horror game, but from time to time it's nice to have more psycholgical game sessions, and not about &quot;monster of the week&quot;. I think that &quot;social hunt&quot; like trying to bulid homeless house could be very intersting this kind of thing. Or negoations between the packs. You know - social scenarios, not &quot;we will destroy next spirit/Host/Claimed/Pure&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T13:06:37-07:00","id":120476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120470#post120470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so if I get it too literally, why each Tribe has <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/houses-of-the-moon/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;favored enemy&quot;</a>? Only Iron Masters have thing I could assume is concept - they are hunting organisations, religions, etc. - but rest have spirits or spirits based hybrids ( werewolves are also this one ). What can I thought other from the info we get?<br /> <br /> If we get something like that Tribes takes abstracs also as they Hunts, I could see something like Strom Lords hunting imputyies in society, Blood Talons weak elements, etc. Then &quot;social hunting&quot; Strom Lord that runs homeless shelter would have sens and show &quot;social hunting&quot;, making also character that aren't all about going after monsters in the night.<br /> <br /> What I mean, basiclly, is this - I see there is huge empathies on Uratha spirit side and duties. But there isn't very much hilighted they flesh/human side a bit. I know it's action horror game, but from time to time it's nice to have more psycholgical game sessions, and not about &quot;monster of the week&quot;. I think that &quot;social hunt&quot; like trying to bulid homeless house could be very intersting this kind of thing. Or negoations between the packs. You know - social scenarios, not &quot;we will destroy next spirit/Host/Claimed/Pure&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>All tribes have concepts. The whole &quot;favored enemy&quot; thing is an addition to the concepts of the tribes, not a replacement.<br /> <br /> If one doesn't know how to run Werewolf: the Forsaken without resorting to the monster of the week thing, then 1) I recommend instantly checking out my 1001 story hooks thread and 2) this really, <i>really</i> isn't the fault of the game. It's a whole lot deeper than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 04-27-2014, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T13:12:58-07:00","id":120477,"title":"","content":"A &quot;hunt&quot;, in the context of Werewolf: the Forsaken, isn't just about a chase scene and a combat scene, and blammo - the session is over.<br /> <br /> If your prey is a Bale Hound masquerading as the leader of your allied pack, but you're the only ones who know about it, then the hunt will require a great deal of investigation and social interaction.<br /> <br /> If your prey is a powerful spirit of poverty in a city in a dire financial situation, then you can't kill it with your claws. As long as you don't solve the core underlying problem in the Flesh, if you kill the spirit, it'll will just come back again and again.<br /> <br /> If your prey is a spider who hides in the brain of a person for a few days and then moves on to the next, then good luck finding the spider without some heavy investigation and spiritual skills.<br /> <br /> If your prey is a Ridden schoolteacher who passes on a legacy of hate and pain to a new generation of kids, then the hunt will require all sorts of social interaction and subtlety.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> This is the sort of thing that's explained in detail in the Werewolf: the Forsaken <b>corebook</b>, and, presumably, in the Idigam Chronicle book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 04-27-2014, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T13:29:53-07:00","id":120489,"title":"","content":"Just because the tribes have favored prey does not mean they don't hunt anything else. Everything a werewolf does is a hunt, everything a werewolf interacts with, whether socially, mentally, or physically is its prey. That's just how werewolves are wired to think. The favored prey is the target of the siskur-dah, a ritualistic hunt that the Uratha perform. But just because you're not actively partaking in the sacred hunt doesn't mean you're not hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:28:00-07:00","id":120532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120477#post120477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;hunt&quot;, in the context of Werewolf: the Forsaken, isn't just about a chase scene and a combat scene, and blammo - the session is over.</div> </div> </div> </div>To draw a connection:<br /> <br /> The Forsaken share their basic worldview with the Shadow. In that ecosystem, every spirit is either predator or prey.<br /> <br /> This does not mean that bank-spirits sprout ephemeral claws and fangs and run down Shadow-Main Street snapping at the heels of money-spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:38:38-07:00","id":120543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120532#post120532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To draw a connection:<br /> <br /> The Forsaken share their basic worldview with the Shadow. In that ecosystem, every spirit is either predator or prey.<br /> <br /> This does not mean that bank-spirits sprout ephemeral claws and fangs and run down Shadow-Main Street snapping at the heels of money-spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair? they spin marketing like a carnivorous flower lays out a sweet scent to attract insects, waits for them to land on it and then snaps it's jaws (vault door) closed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T14:55:00-07:00","id":120558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120543#post120543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair? they spin marketing like a carnivorous flower lays out a sweet scent to attract insects, waits for them to land on it and then snaps it's jaws (vault door) closed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T06:56:13-07:00","id":120914,"title":"","content":"I like what I'm seeing here and I guess this is one of those cases where I always read it as the Cahalith being the over-the-top (potential) glory hounds, so it doesn't look like that big a change to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T07:53:29-07:00","id":120932,"title":"","content":"The way I see the over-the-top-glory-hound thing is that the Cahalith are all about stories, and they naturally want to be the main character in the stories they create. They want their deeds to be remembered, so they tend a little towards the extravagant .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T08:43:06-07:00","id":120954,"title":"","content":"Eh. I always preferred the &quot;heart of the pack&quot; as well as the prophet angles of the Gibbous Moons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:03:02-07:00","id":120964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120954#post120954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I always preferred the &quot;heart of the pack&quot; as well as the prophet angles of the Gibbous Moons.</div> </div> </div> </div>You technically still can since the glory hound presented can be looked at as a single aspect of many roles in a story. Perhaps when you play, you are the Cahalith who moves the story forward by helping the others while you take a supporting role to well...support the flow of the story to how it should end","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T09:29:25-07:00","id":120979,"title":"","content":"I think the write up leaves plenty of room for Cahalith to be the heart of the pack. I actually appreciate the slight change though. The write-up posits them as far more the &quot;glue&quot; of the pack that socially holds it all together. This could be &quot;the heart&quot; but it can be expressed in other ways as well. It allows greater flexibility of roles in the social dynamic of the pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T10:50:26-07:00","id":121039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices#post119420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/structure-and-moon-signs/\" target=\"_blank\">Find Your Fate Here</a><br /> <br /> Oh my beloved Cahalith, how terrifying you have become. Take me in your arms that will break me again and and again, and show me just how long those teeth really are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I die laughing !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:01:34-07:00","id":121046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=120932#post120932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I see the over-the-top-glory-hound thing is that the Cahalith are all about stories, and they naturally want to be the main character in the stories they create. They want their deeds to be remembered, so they tend a little towards the extravagant .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree with this. Sure, a lot of Cahalith want to be the main characters in the stories, but ego trips aren't a necessary consequence of seeing the world through the lens of story. There's also the desire to create drama for the sake of resolving it; if the drama is already there, then the next phase of the story is figuring out what to do about it. Of course, if it's <i>not</i> there, then the story is boring, forgettable, and needs some shaking up. Why wouldn't a Cahalith play the Obi-Wan to his Rahu's Luke? &quot;Of course I'm making a heroic sacrifice. That's what mentors do in stories!&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm trying to say is... They can also be Elan from Order of the Stick, if you read that. Especially strip #916.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-28T11:47:48-07:00","id":121076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/119420-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-auspices?p=121046#post121046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure I agree with this. Sure, a lot of Cahalith want to be the main characters in the stories, but ego trips aren't a necessary consequence of seeing the world through the lens of story. There's also the desire to create drama for the sake of resolving it; if the drama is already there, then the next phase of the story is figuring out what to do about it. Of course, if it's <i>not</i> there, then the story is boring, forgettable, and needs some shaking up. Why wouldn't a Cahalith play the Obi-Wan to his Rahu's Luke? &amp;quot;Of course I'm making a heroic sacrifice. That's what mentors do in stories!&amp;quot; I guess what I'm trying to say is... They can also be Elan from Order of the Stick, if you read that. Especially strip #916.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very true. And the write up does account for the fact that not all Cahalith are unsubtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}